# php-7.1-minimal.patch
# CVE-2026-109618 / CVE-2026-109619 ("php2shell") MINIMAL backport for PHP 7.1.x
# (tested on php-7.1.9, the version shipped in
#  registry.api.weibo.com/csmonitor/php_base.php71:1.10-1.12)
#
# Official PHP-group approach, ported from php-7.2-minimal.patch
# (php2shell-patches repo). Conservative fix:
#
#  1. OOM bailout -> fprintf(stderr) + _exit(1) (CVE-2026-109618):
#     zend_mm_safe_error_ex() replaces zend_error_noreturn() + longjmp
#     in every "Possible integer overflow" path; the process dies
#     immediately, partially-initialised request state is never consumed.
#  2. Force-disable session upload progress (CVE-2026-109619):
#     `if (!PS(rfc1867_enabled) || 1)` in php_session_rfc1867_callback().
#     One line, breaks the confirmed UAF consumer path.
#     NOTE: session.upload_progress is now ALWAYS off — progress bars
#     stop working. Use php-7.1-enhanced-universal.patch if you need them.
#  3. Limit retained multipart headers (main/rfc1867.c): keep only
#     Content-Disposition and Content-Type, so an attacker cannot exhaust
#     memory_limit with hundreds of thousands of headers. Also adds the
#     size_t substring_conf fixup and the max_multipart_body_parts ini
#     (default -1 = max_input_vars + max_file_uploads).
#  4. Reset globals between requests (CVE-2026-109619): clear error
#     handlers, exception handlers, http_globals (ZVAL_UNDEF), object
#     store, last-error state and SAPI request_info pointers at shutdown;
#     zend_llist head/tail reset; array_init_singleton() in GPC parsing.
#
# Differences from the 7.2 minimal patch (7.1 adaptations):
#  - ext/session/session.c: `|| true` -> `|| 1` — PHP 7.1's session.c
#    does not include stdbool.h (7.2 does), so the C keyword `true`
#    does not compile there.
#  - Zend/zend_execute_API.c: 7.1's shutdown_executor() has a different
#    layout (no fast_shutdown branch near the end); the EG(error_handling) /
#    EG(exception) / objects_store resets are placed at the end of
#    shutdown_executor(), mirroring where 7.2 puts them.
#  - Zend/zend_alloc.c: 7.1 has no integer-overflow check inside
#    zend_mm_realloc_heap(); the check is added at the
#    _zend_mm_realloc/_zend_mm_realloc2 entry points instead
#    (uses ZEND_SIZE_MAX / ZEND_MM_OVERHEAD so it compiles both with
#    and without ZEND_DEBUG).
#  - main/php_variables.c: the fourth array_init() call site needed the
#    same array_init_singleton() rename (context differs from 7.2).
#
# Apply with: patch -p1 < php-7.1-minimal.patch
#   (or: git apply php-7.1-minimal.patch — the base image 1.11+ has git
#    but no `patch` rpm)
#
# Verified on php-7.1.9 with the image toolchain (gcc 10.2.1):
#  - applies cleanly to the pristine php.net tarball
#  - buildconf + configure + make -> success
#  - OOM triggers _exit(1) (exit code 1, no bailout)
#  - upload progress is inert even with session.upload_progress.enabled=1
#    (no upload_progress_key written to the session file)
#  - multipart upload still works; max_multipart_body_parts=2 truncates
#    a 3-part body with the official warning
#
